  "explanation": {
    "en": "誰 (だれ) means “who.” It is used to ask about people. You can use it with particles like が, は, に, と to ask about the subject, topic, or person involved.\n\nKey points:\n• 誰が = who (subject)\n• 誰ですか = who is it\n• 誰と = who with\n• Polite form: どなた (more formal)\n\nExample: “あの人は誰ですか” means “Who is that person?” “誰と行きますか” means “Who will you go with?”\n\nWhen asking politely, you can use どなた, but 誰 is common and natural in everyday conversation.\n\nPractice by asking about people around you: 誰が先生ですか, 誰と勉強しますか.",
    "ja": ""
  },
